@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-service`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-service.l4 (section 7 of the Interpretation Act 1978).
--
-- Every expected value was decided by reading section 7 and written down before the module was run. A failing assertion is a
-- finding; no expected value is edited to match the code. The section has no figure for the "ordinary course of post", so the
-- fixtures supply the time (12 March 2026, 09:30) and the tests assert that the module hands it back, never computes it.

§ `Fixtures: the letter, and each way it can differ from a properly posted one`

`a properly posted letter` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter where no Act requires service by post` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS FALSE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter where a contrary intention appears` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS TRUE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter that is not properly addressed` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS FALSE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter that is not pre-paid` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS FALSE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter that is not posted` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS FALSE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter that does not contain the document` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS FALSE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a letter where the contrary is proved` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS TRUE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 12, `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 30)

`a properly posted letter with no ordinary-course time supplied` MEANS `A letter served by post` WITH
    `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the letter is properly addressed` IS TRUE
    `the letter is pre-paid` IS TRUE
    `the letter is posted` IS TRUE
    `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS FALSE
    `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS NOTHING

§ `Section 7 applies, and when it does not`

-- "Where an Act authorises or requires any document to be served by post (whether the expression 'serve' or ... 'give' or 'send' or any other expression is used)".
#ASSERT `section 7 applies to` `a properly posted letter`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 applies to` `a letter where no Act requires service by post`
-- "unless the contrary intention appears".
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 applies to` `a letter where a contrary intention appears`

§ `Posting a properly addressed, pre-paid letter containing the document is deemed service`

#ASSERT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a properly posted letter`
-- Each of the four ways of failing: addressed, pre-paid, posted, containing the document.
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter that is not properly addressed`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter that is not pre-paid`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter that is not posted`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter that does not contain the document`
-- Where the section does not apply, it deems nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter where no Act requires service by post`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter where a contrary intention appears`
-- A letter whose time is in dispute is still deemed to be service: only the time is affected.
#ASSERT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` `a letter where the contrary is proved`

§ `The time at which service is deemed effected`

-- "to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post".
#ASSERT (`section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a properly posted letter`)'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 12)
#ASSERT (`section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a properly posted letter`)'s `the hour` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT (`section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a properly posted letter`)'s `the minute` EQUALS 30
-- "unless the contrary is proved": the section does not say what time then governs.
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter where the contrary is proved` BECAUSE "section 7 says the deemed time yields to proof of the contrary and does not say what time then governs"
-- No ordinary-course time supplied: the Act has no figure.
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a properly posted letter with no ordinary-course time supplied` BECAUSE "the Interpretation Act 1978 does not say how long the ordinary course of post takes, so the caller must supply when the letter would be delivered"
-- Where service is not deemed, the section gives no time.
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter that is not properly addressed` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter that is not pre-paid` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter that is not posted` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter that does not contain the document` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter where no Act requires service by post` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` `a letter where a contrary intention appears` BECAUSE "section 7 does not deem service to be effected by this letter, so it gives no time of service"
